# .env.dev — minimal DEV-lane environment (SEC-5)
#
# Purpose: lane worktrees read THIS file instead of the live stack's real
# `.env`, so dev/test code never holds provider secrets it does not need.
#   - dev lanes mock every provider call (tests) => NO keys required
#   - NO GROQ / GITHUB / any cloud key lives here (packet rule)
#   - values stay EMPTY: presence-checking code treats empty as absent
# Real keys stay ONLY in the live-stack process's .env (mode 600, owner
# only — see scripts/SECRETS.md; doctor verifies).
#
# Create/refresh:  scripts/install-env-dev.sh   (mode 600, idempotent)

# --- provider slots (deliberately empty; add NOTHING cloud-shaped here) ---
# (none — everything is mocked in dev)

# --- non-secret knobs dev lanes may flip locally (examples) ---
# RAPHAEL_LOG_LEVEL=debug
# RAPHAEL_INSTANCE=        # set per-lane when running anything parallel
